{"id":"u-51f88736-30bf-4bbd-af0e-76c7265af01c","src":"community","title":"Veteran Strength","author":"Anthony Caravaggi","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/pt4eDV-veteran-strength","desc":"Veteran Strength is a 12-week training block for experienced lifters and older athletes who already have a solid strength base and now need a smarter way to maintain it, improve body composition, and stay healthy while training hard.\n\nThis program is not about chasing constant personal records. It’s about preserving strength, refining performance, and improving physique without accumulating unnecessary fatigue or joint stress. Success for experienced lifters comes from better training decisions, not more effort. Veteran Strength is built for that phase.\n\nThe program is designed for lifters who:\n- have years of consistent training\n- achieved meaningful strength levels\n- want to maintain or slightly improve strength while losing fat\n- need structured training that manages fatigue intelligently\n- value longevity as much as performance\n\nThere are four phases:\nPhase 1 (weeks 1–4): build consistency and work capacity\nPhase 2 (weeks 5–8): productive overload with controlled intensity\nPhase 3 (week 9): fatigue reset and recovery\nPhase 4 (weeks 10–12): performance rebound and strength consolidation\n\nThe program uses RPE-based autoregulation, allowing training to adapt to daily readiness, recovery, and stress levels. Training focuses on heavy compound lifts to maintain maximal strength,  hypertrophy work for muscle retention and physique development,  machines and cables to increase volume without excess joint stress and carries and core work for stability and resilience. Conditioning is used strategically to support fat loss, cardiovascular health, and recovery, without interfering with strength performance.\n\nBy the end of the cycle, the expectation is not just maintained strength, but improved training efficiency, better recovery, and (with the right nutrition and recovery schedule) a more athletic, defined physique.","level":["Intermediate","Advanced"],"goals":["Muscle","Strength"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":2,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-07-06T07:57:36.512Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Day 1","Day 2","Day 3"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Bench Press (Paused)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7},{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6,"x":2}]},{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Dip (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Tricep Rope Push Down (Cable)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Fly (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Ab Wheel","sets":[{"amrap":1}]},{"n":"Cardio","sets":[{"sec":600,"secHi":900}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7},{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6,"x":2}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Supported Row (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown (Neutral Grip)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Rear Delt Fly (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Pull-Up (Weighted)","sets":[{"amrap":1}]},{"n":"Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Ab Wheel","sets":[{"amrap":1}]},{"n":"Cardio","sets":[{"sec":600,"secHi":900}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Overhead Press (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":8,"rpe":7},{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":6,"x":2}]},{"n":"Upright Row (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Arnold Press","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Hack Squat","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Lying Leg Curl","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Incline Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"n":"Dip (Bodyweight)","sets":[{"amrap":1,"rpe":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Ab Wheel","sets":[{"amrap":1}]},{"n":"Cardio